{"id": "b2065319-a24b-4ea5-bcba-49f344f9729a", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Actually, missing serverSideEncryptionConfiguration doesn't mean unencrypted — that field applies to managed KBs, while for VECTOR KBs it's not applicable since encryption at rest defaults to an AWS-owned key. So this should really be marked PASS or "not applicable" rather than a violation, unless the policy specifically mandates a customer-managed key.

The real encryption posture lives in the OpenSearch Serverless collection's encryption policy (always encrypted, AWS-owned or CMK) and the S3 data source bucket — I should recommend checking those instead of overclaiming based on this field alone.

"}]}
